## Maintenance plan boundaries

Reviewed against d71d343 (#67). The owner wants smaller, independently reviewable
changes that reduce duplicated responsibilities. This does not authorize executing
the backlog. Each maintenance task should name the behavior preserved, the code or
responsibilities removed, and the places future changes must touch. Count implementation
growth separately from tests/generated files; do not delete regression coverage to meet
a line-count target. Moving the same responsibilities into more files is not success.

Recommended order: mod-operation-failure-contract, i18n-english-only-enforcement,
i18n-maintenance-audit, shared-install-prompt-flow. Treat these as separate tasks.
Keep #65's game declarations and validation. Expand their schema, generators, adapters
or hooks only for a current game requirement or demonstrated duplication to remove.
Older architecture proposals below remain conditional, not a mandate for a rewrite.

