## TODO: shared-install-prompt-flow

BrowsePage, ModDetailPage, modDetail/DownloadsTab, hooks/useModActions and UpdatesModal
repeat archive-picker, host-pack, Crime Boss flat-confirmation and unrecognized-archive
state/wiring. installSentinels.ts dispatches outcomes but does not own their lifecycle.
Inspect FileSelectModal's paused loop and drag/drop entry points before setting scope.

Proposed shape: one shared hook for an active installation conversation and one component
rendering its prompt. Callers supply existing installation work/context; the shared flow
owns prompt resolution, cancellation and completion. Batch updates retain their queue
and await the same interaction. Choose placement from actual concurrency/navigation
needs, not a process-global single-install lock or generic workflow registry.

Preserve source acquisition (including free Nexus nxm handoff), loader routing, Crime
Boss target/skeleton rules, host packs, automatic update variant matching, secondary
targets, progress, partial failure reporting and installed-list refresh. Staged handles
retain backend authorization/ownership and cleanup on completion/cancel. Cancellation
must not leave a queue or Promise stuck. No new sources or Rust install redesign here.

Migrate in reviewable slices and delete each caller's replaced state, handlers and modal
wiring in that slice. Done means a new prompt needs one owner changed, not every entry
point. Verify single/reinstall/per-file installs, batch pause/resume/cancel, navigation
and concurrent requests, preserving domain-specific tests.

