## TODO: nexus-feature-parity

Nexus works but is narrower than ModWorkshop. This is the FUNCTIONAL gap list, separate
from the architecture work (which is done): the domain model, typed IPC and the shared
Browse page all landed 2026-07-20.

VERIFIED 2026-08-07 by live GraphQL introspection plus targeted data queries
(unauthenticated but app-identified, the mode the 2026-07-29 research validated; this
machine has no Nexus sign-in, so anything marked doc-verified below still needs one
live confirmation from a signed-in session during implementation). Two assumptions
this entry used to state are now WRONG and are corrected here:

1. "Nexus has NO batch metadata endpoint" is FALSE for GraphQL v2. `modsByUid(uids:
   [ID!], offset, count)` and `modFilesByUid(...)` exist and work: uid is
   gameId * 2^32 + modId (confirmed live: uid 29824252903431 = game 6944, mod 7), and
   one request returned several mods' name/version/updatedAt. The nexusModCache
   one-mod-per-2s trickle and the per-mod detail loop in useModData's Nexus branch can
   both collapse into one batched query per game. See nexus-update-detection.
2. "The GraphQL search selection carries no version" is no longer true of the schema:
   Mod.version is NON_NULL and returns real data in the mods search (verified live,
   "3.11"). The empty-version behavior is now a selection choice in nexus.rs's
   SEARCH_QUERY, not an API limit. Fixing it must be coordinated with useModData's
   empty-version-suppresses-update-prompts rule so cached search results do not start
   nagging (see nexus-update-detection).

### Dependencies: structured data EXISTS on v2 (was: assumed site-only)

`Mod.modRequirements` is real: `nexusRequirements` (paginated nodes of `{ modId,
gameId, modName, notes, url, externalRequirement }`), `dlcRequirements`, and
`modsRequiringThisMod`. That is exactly the split DepsTab needs: internal requirements
carry a real modId/gameId to open in-app, external ones carry url + name for the gated
external-link row, notes is the author's free text. Shape verified live; both sampled
mods had totalCount 0, so POPULATION is unverified - before building, find one mod
whose site page lists requirements and confirm the API returns them (open question 6
in nexus-policy-boundaries if it does not).

Scope guidance when built: DISPLAY first (a Nexus deps tab mirroring DepsTab, with
external rows opening through shell_open_external). Auto-install of internal
requirements can reuse the existing per-source install flow afterward; do not build
recursive tree resolution up front - batch modsByUid makes enrichment cheap, but the
tree is still author-declared data of unknown consistency. No "optional vs required"
flag exists; the site's optional grouping is not in the schema - never invent one from
notes text. DepsTab's `(!m.source || m.source === 'modworkshop')` guard stays until
this lands; unresolved is still more honest than mis-resolved.

### Explicitly NOT doing: category and tag filtering

Owner decision 2026-07-20, after checking the API docs. Do not reopen this.

For the record, since the docs suggest it might be technically possible: the v2 `mods`
query takes `facets` (type ModsFacet) alongside `filter`, and the schema carries a
`modCategory` field and a full `categories` query, so some form of category narrowing
likely exists server-side. It is still not worth building. Nexus categories are a
different taxonomy from ModWorkshop's (different ids, names, hierarchy, per-game
associations), so the two could never share one dropdown, and each source would need its
own filter UI for little gain. (2026-08-07 re-introspection confirmed modCategory, tags,
and a nameStemmed search filter all exist and return live data; the decision above is
about product value, not availability, and stands.)

### Verified lower-priority surface (available, deliberately not scheduled)

All confirmed by introspection 2026-08-07. None of these outranks the entries below or
the stalker2-support sequencing; they are recorded so nobody re-researches them.

- Endorse/abstain: v2 mutations createModEndorsement / abstainFromModEndorsement (and
  v1 REST endorse.json). v1 docs describe not-downloaded / too-soon error cases -
  confirm exact rules when built and surface them as friendly messages, never as raw
  errors.
- Tracking: v2 trackMod / untrackMod mutations plus Mod.viewerTracked. Enables a
  "track on Nexus" toggle and a tracked-mods import ("bring your Nexus library") -
  needs an authed query for the user's tracked list (introspect when built; v1 REST
  /user/tracked_mods.json exists as fallback).
- Uploader metadata: Mod.uploader { name, memberId, avatar } returns live data;
  profile URL derivable as nexusmods.com/users/{memberId}. Small detail-page row.
- Collections: full v2 read surface exists (collection, collectionsV2,
  collectionRevision). RESEARCH ONLY - large, Vortex-flagship territory; nothing in
  Modrex needs it today, and it must not enter the roadmap before the mod.io work has
  real consumers (see acquire-install-split sequencing).
- Media section: the v2 media query is the per-game community media browser
  (game-scoped filter only - NOT a mod's gallery; see nexus-detail-parity for that
  verdict).
- Persistent Nexus caching: nexusModCache is deliberately session-only; keys are
  already game-scoped, so localStorage persistence mirroring modCache is possible any
  time. Low value until the batched update check (nexus-update-detection) settles what
  is worth persisting.

