## TODO: nexus-premium-downloads

Premium accounts should download inside the app; free accounts keep the website
handoff. Tier detection first, direct downloads second. Status: ready to implement
except the two live confirmations marked below. VERIFIED/doc-verified 2026-08-07.

User problem: Premium users currently get the same browser round-trip as free users,
although the API supports direct links for them; and Modrex cannot even say which tier
the signed-in account is.

Tier detection - two verified candidates, pick during implementation:

- OIDC userinfo endpoint (https://users.nexusmods.com/oauth/userinfo, live-verified to
  exist via discovery): claims include membership_roles and premium_expiry. OAuth-native,
  no v1 dependency. Response shape untested (no sign-in on the dev machine).
- v1 /users/validate.json (doc-verified via Nexus's node-nexus-api types): is_premium,
  is_supporter, user name. CAUTION: the response also carries the account's personal
  api key and email - never log the response body, store only the booleans + name.

Cache the result per session plus on sign-in; a detection failure degrades to the free
flow silently is WRONG - show "tier unknown, using website flow" instead, since a
Premium user silently demoted would report it as a download bug.

Direct downloads (Premium only):

- nexus_get_download_link already accepts (None, None) for key/expires; that keyless
  call is Premium-only BY DESIGN - free accounts 403 (confirmed live during the nxm
  work; the first-party node-nexus-api docs state the key "can only be generated on
  the website" for non-premium). LIVE-CONFIRM once with a Premium session: keyless
  link succeeds under the OAuth bearer, and note the returned link's expiry behavior
  (links are temporary; treat a failed download start as expired -> re-request once).
- Flow: DownloadsTab install button, when tier == premium, resolves the link and runs
  the normal download_file + install pipeline (progress events already exist); free
  tier keeps the nmm=1 website handoff and the nxm:// path untouched. Respect
  Mod.directDownloadEnabled if it proves relevant to per-mod availability.
- Cancellation/retry: download_file has progress but no user cancel; acceptable for
  v1 of this feature, note S2-sized files will eventually want cancel + resume.

Modules: nexus.rs, DownloadsTab.tsx, SettingsPage (tier row), settings cache. Tests:
tier parse (userinfo and/or validate fixtures), keyless-link request shape, free-tier
routing regression (must still open the website). Error cases: 403 on keyless call for
a free account must route to the website flow with no error toast (it is the expected
tier behavior), expired link -> one silent re-request then a real error.

Non-goals, permanent: no free-tier workaround of any kind - no scraping, no browser
automation, no reusing another session's key. The website click IS the free-tier
authorization, per Nexus's design. See nexus-policy-boundaries.

