## TODO: nexus-oauth-lifecycle

Small verified auth gaps. VERIFIED 2026-08-07 against
users.nexusmods.com/.well-known/openid-configuration.

- Revocation: a revocation_endpoint EXISTS (/oauth/revoke). nexus_oauth_sign_out
  currently deletes local tokens only - add a best-effort revoke call (access +
  refresh token, per RFC 7009 token_type_hint) before local deletion. Failure to
  revoke must not block sign-out. There is NO end_session endpoint - nothing else to
  call.
- Refresh rotation: UNRESOLVED - discovery metadata does not say whether refresh
  tokens rotate. Keep REFRESH_LOCK's conservative serialize-everything behavior, and
  NEVER refresh the app's grant from outside the app (a rotated token persisted
  nowhere would sign the real app out) - this is also why verification sessions must
  not "just refresh" an expired token.
- Scopes: keep exactly `public openid profile`. Discovery advertises only
  public/openid; profile was granted at registration (support-confirmed) and feeds
  the settings display. Nothing verified this session needs a new scope - endorse/
  track/collections mutations should be re-tested under the current scopes before
  assuming otherwise.

