## TODO: sources-module-restructure

Deferred source architecture proposal. Revalidate its scope against the maintenance
boundaries above: do not introduce the full trait or move both clients merely to make
the directories symmetrical. Implement only boundaries a current source feature needs
or that demonstrably eliminate repeated behavior.

### Context

`api.rs` is a single-host client: modworkshop BASE url, a process-global rate
limiter tuned to modworkshop's undocumented 90 req/min shared budget,
x-ratelimit-remaining semantics, register_download. `nexus.rs` (post-merge) is a
second free-standing client. The proven structural pattern for "several
implementations of one concept" in this codebase is `launchers/` (types.rs trait +
one file per implementation).

### What to do

- NOTE (2026-07-20): `commands/sources.rs` ALREADY EXISTS as the source registry
  (which sources exist, which games each serves, the id each knows a game by, plus
  the list_sources command the renderer reads). Creating a `sources/` directory
  collides with it, so absorb it: `sources/mod.rs` re-exports the registry, and the
  per-source clients sit beside it. Do not start a second parallel concept.
- Create `src-tauri/src/commands/sources/` mirroring `launchers/`: a ModSource
  trait (list/search, get detail, files, request-download, rate policy, auth
  needs), `modworkshop.rs` and `nexus.rs` as the two implementations. Per-source
  rate limiter instances instead of the global statics (keep the HTTP_CLIENT
  invariant: one shared reqwest client for everything).
- requestPriority.ts foreground/background arbitration currently assumes one
  shared rate-limited pipe; make it per-source. Still true as of 2026-08-01: the
  file's own header comment says "rate-limited connection to modworkshop" and it
  has no notion of a source.
- New source credentials must reuse commands/secrets.rs, including the existing
  explicitly surfaced settings.json fallback when the credential store is unavailable.
- Thumbnails: `thumbnails.rs` hardcodes storage.modworkshop.net and keys the disk
  cache by CDN filename (unique only within that CDN). Key by full-URL hash
  instead; every new source's image CDN origin must be added to BOTH `csp` and
  `devCsp` in tauri.conf.json (a miss fails silently as blank images).

